        "title": "Calculate f(x+h) - f(x)",
        "text": "$f(x+h) - f(x)$\\n\\n$= (3x^2 + 6xh + 3h^2 - 2x - 2h + 1) - (3x^2 - 2x + 1)$\\n\\n$= 3x^2 + 6xh + 3h^2 - 2x - 2h + 1 - 3x^2 + 2x - 1$\\n\\n$= 6xh + 3h^2 - 2h$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "DBE NSC Paper 1",
        "license": "Public Domain"
    },
    {
        "id": "calc-derivative-001b-h2",
        "type": "hint",
        "dependencies": ["calc-derivative-001b-h1"],
        "title": "Divide by h and Factor",
        "text": "$\\frac{f(x+h) - f(x)}{h} = \\frac{6xh + 3h^2 - 2h}{h}$\\n\\nFactor out $h$:\\n\\n$= \\frac{h(6x + 3h - 2)}{h} = 6x + 3h - 2$",
        "variabilization": {},
        "oer": "DBE NSC Paper 1",
        "license": "Public Domain"
    },
    {
        "id": "calc-derivative-001b-h3",
        "type": "scaffold",
        "problemType": "TextBox",
        "answerType": "string",
        "hintAnswer": ["6x-2"],
        "dependencies": ["calc-derivative-001b-h2"],
        "title": "Take the Limit",
        "text": "$f'(x) = \\lim_{h \\to 0}(6x + 3h - 2)$\\n\\nAs $h \\to 0$:\\n\\n$f'(x) = 6x + 0 - 2 = 6x - 2$\\n\\nNote: Using the power rule: $\\frac{d}{dx}(3x^2 - 2x + 1) = 6x - 2$ ✓",
